---
import { AGENDA } from "../../../../lib/contact";
import StudioLayout from "../../../../layouts/StudioLayout.astro";
import LabNav from "../../../../components/studio/LabNav.astro";
import DerniersArticles from "../../../../components/studio/DerniersArticles.astro";
---
<StudioLayout
  titre="Harness"
  description="The tool we are building to know what an automated process does, and to be able to prove it."
  actif=""
  fil={[{ libelle: "Lab", href: "/en/lab/" }, { libelle: "Harness" }]}>
<section class="hero">
  <div class="wrap prose">
    <p class="eyebrow">Lab · Internal tool</p>
    <h1>Know what a system does, and be able to prove it.</h1>
    <p class="lead">Harness is the tool we are building to verify what an automated process does. It maps the process from its actual runs and checks that every expected behaviour holds.</p>
    <LabNav courant="presentation" />
  </div>
</section>

<section>
  <div class="wrap prose">
    <h2>Why we are building it</h2>
    <p>Our method promises to measure what agents produce. That promise only holds if we can say, at any moment, what an automated process actually does: which rules it applies, which exceptions it escalates, what it does when a piece of data is missing.</p>
    <p>Conventional tests tell you a program doesn&rsquo;t crash. Harness checks what it does: the rules applied, the edge cases, the deviations from the specification. <strong>It serves our own deliveries first.</strong></p>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="tint">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="prose"><h2>What it does</h2></div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card">
        <p class="who">See</p>
        <h3>The map of the process</h3>
        <p>The steps, rules, exceptions and their dependencies, taken from the process&rsquo;s actual runs.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="card">
        <p class="who">Change</p>
        <h3>What a change affects</h3>
        <p>Before changing a rule, you see what it touches. The change is proposed, then reviewed by someone before it goes out.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="card">
        <p class="who">Verify</p>
        <h3>What holds, and what doesn&rsquo;t</h3>
        <p>Every expected behaviour is verified. Gaps are named, with where they occur, before they cost anything.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <p style="margin-top:32px"><a href="/en/lab/harness/how-it-works/">How it works, screen by screen, on a customer order &rarr;</a></p>
  </div>
</section>

<section>
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="prose">
      <h2>Where it fits in the method</h2>
      <p>Harness equips three of the four stages of <a href="/en/method/">our method</a>.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="steps">
      <div class="step"><div class="n">2</div><div>
        <h3><a href="/en/method/#fondation">Foundation</a></h3>
        <p>Map what exists before touching it: what the process really does, exceptions included.</p>
      </div></div>
      <div class="step"><div class="n">3</div><div>
        <h3><a href="/en/method/#deploiement">Deployment</a></h3>
        <p>Show what a change affects before it goes into production, and have it reviewed by the person accountable for it.</p>
      </div></div>
      <div class="step"><div class="n">4</div><div>
        <h3><a href="/en/method/#pilotage">Oversight and verification</a></h3>
        <p>Continuously verify that every expected behaviour holds. The quarterly report is built on these checks.</p>
      </div></div>
    </div>
    <div class="note prose">
      <strong>Status</strong>
      <p>Harness is not for sale. We are building it for our missions and open it to a few teams we choose.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<DerniersArticles etiquette="harness" titre="What we write about it" />

<section class="cta">
  <div class="wrap">
    <h2>What the method would do for you</h2>
    <p>45 minutes to find out whether it&rsquo;s worth it for your processes.</p>
    <div class="btn-row">
      <a class="btn" href={AGENDA} target="_blank" rel="noopener">Book a call</a>
      <a class="btn btn-ghost" href="/en/method/">See the method</a>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
</StudioLayout>
